<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Safaviyya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Safaviyya Sufi order, Safaviyya order</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Safaviyya was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> religious order founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safi-al-din-ardabili">Safi al-Din Ardabili</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the late thirteenth or early fourteenth century. Over time it became increasingly militant and Shia in orientation and gained a devoted following among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> tribes known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a>. The order's leaders used this following to found the Safavid state in 1501.</p></div>
